# Fixed defect 2431, 2026-11-10, lane b30-pkg: inside the package `json`,
# whose own catalogue names `core`, `use core` and `use core/strconv`, the
# brackets forgotten (spec § 1: inside a package a `use` starts at the
# package's own root, and its brackets name entries of the package's own
# catalogue).
#
# SYMPTOM: both told `unknown_package_module`, the package `json` has no
# module `core`, with no word of the entry, where the same two lines in the
# program's own file are told the entry and `use <core>/strconv` (defect
# 2394's repair, panel 235's R18).
#
# CAUSE: a bare `use` of a package's file names a module of that package, so
# `modules.unknown_modules` handed it to `package_told.unknown`, which never
# asked a catalogue; R18's question was asked of the program's files alone.
#
# FIX: the same message, then that `core` is an entry of `json`'s own
# catalogue, asked through the aliases discovery mapped from it: the whole
# entry is offered the modules at its root, and `use core/strconv` is told
# `package_unmarked`, `use <core>/strconv`, the repair certain in a folder of
# the author's own. The modules are `vendor/json/parse.hero` and
# `vendor/json/parse2.hero`, each marked where it is told.
use <json>/parse
use <json>/parse2

function main()
    print(parse.word() + parse2.word())
